  "description_short": "Heritage railway station turned family restaurant serving hearty South African fare in Hartenbos.",
  "description_long": "Housed in Hartenbos's charming old railway station on Port Natal Avenue, Die Stasie brings warmth and nostalgia to every meal. The heritage building sets the tone for honest, home-style cooking that celebrates local flavours and generous portions.\n\nThe menu leans into South African comfort food, with dishes that feel like Sunday lunch at your ouma's house. Expect proper steaks, traditional potjiekos, and plates piled high with all the trimmings. The relaxed atmosphere makes it easy for families to settle in, and the historic setting adds character without feeling stuffy.\n\nLocated in the heart of Hartenbos, just minutes from the beach, Die Stasie serves as both a neighbourhood gathering spot and a discovery for visitors exploring Mossel Bay's coastal suburbs. It's the kind of place where locals return regularly and holidaymakers stumble upon something genuine.",
